course: dictionary
lesson: 11693
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words wear different coats. Attendant is one of them. As a noun, an attendant is a person whose job is to look after people or a place. «The pool attendant handed me a towel at the door.» The attendant is a worker at the pool, so you can ask them for help.
explain: Attendant can also be an adjective, which is a formal word. It means coming along with something or caused by it. «Cold winds and slippery rocks are attendant risks of the climb.» The risks come with the climb, because the climb causes them.
explain: How do you tell which meaning is which? Ask yourself: is this a person doing a job, or is it describing a thing? If you can put a person in front of it, like a flight attendant or a museum attendant, it is the noun. If it describes risks, problems or dangers, it is the adjective.
fact: An attendant is a person whose job is to look after people or a place.
fact: Examples of attendants are flight attendants, car park attendants and pool attendants.
fact: As an adjective, attendant is formal and means coming along with something or caused by it.
fact: «Attendant risks» are the risks that come with something, such as the risks of a climb.
fact: Check the meaning by swapping in a simple word: a pool attendant is a pool helper, and attendant problems are problems that come with something.
exercise: «The pool attendant handed me a towel at the door.» What is a pool attendant? | A towel that is wet | *A person whose job is to look after the pool | A swimmer who wins races | A type of pool toy
exercise: «Cold winds and slippery rocks are attendant risks of the climb.» What does attendant mean here? | Waiting at the top of the climb | *Coming along with the climb, caused by it | Very old | Friendly and helpful
exercise: «The museum attendant asked us to stay behind the rope.» Find and copy one word that means a person who looks after a place. | museum | *attendant | behind | rope
test: «The flight attendant showed us how to fasten our seat belts.» Who is the flight attendant? | A passenger with a seat belt | A ticket seller at the airport | *A person whose job is to look after passengers on a plane | A pilot who flies the plane
test: «Missing the bus brought attendant problems: a late start and a cross teacher.» What does attendant mean here? | Very old and slow | Waiting in a long line | *Coming along with the problem, caused by it | Pleasant and fun
exam: «The car park attendant waved us into the empty space.» What is the job of a car park attendant? | *Looks after the car park and helps drivers | Repairs the cars | Drives the cars to the garage | Sells the cars
